   ("P3_MAYA", "We've done three rounds of trials, and honestly, the results are all over the place."),
   ("P3_DANIEL", "Which is partly why we wanted to see you. We're not sure whether to write up what we've got or redesign the whole thing."),
   ("P3_TUTOR", "Let's go back a step. Why this experiment in the first place?"),
   ("P3_MAYA", "Well, Daniel wanted it because it's famous."),
   ("P3_DANIEL", "That's not quite fair. What I liked is that people still argue about it. Whether hot water really freezes faster than cold isn't settled, so nobody could accuse us of just confirming a textbook result."),
   ("P3_MAYA", "And the equipment is cheap, although that wasn't really why we chose it."),
   ("P3_TUTOR", "Good. So what's gone wrong?"),
   ("P3_MAYA", "The thing we expected to be a problem was the freezer temperature drifting, so we logged it, and it's actually very stable. The problem is deciding when the water counts as frozen. In round one we went by when ice first appeared on the surface, but that's misleading, because a skin of ice can form while the middle is still liquid."),
   ("P3_DANIEL", "So in round two we put a probe in the centre and called it frozen when that reached zero. But water can supercool. It can sit below zero without turning solid, so that wasn't reliable either."),
   ("P3_TUTOR", "That's the crux of the whole literature, you know. Half the disagreement comes from people defining frozen differently. And round three?"),
   ("P3_DANIEL", "We timed it to complete solidification, judged by the probe reading levelling off after the supercooling dip. The curves are much cleaner."),
   ("P3_TUTOR", "And the result?"),
   ("P3_MAYA", "The hot sample froze first in four of nine pairs. So, no effect, basically."),
   ("P3_TUTOR", "Careful. Nine pairs is a tiny sample. You can say you didn't detect an effect. You can't say there isn't one."),
   ("P3_TUTOR", "Did you check for evaporation? Hot water loses mass."),
   ("P3_DANIEL", "We weighed the containers before and after. The hot samples lost about three per cent."),
   ("P3_MAYA", "We thought about topping them up with extra water, but then it wouldn't be the same sample."),
   ("P3_TUTOR", "Exactly. Don't fiddle with the samples, and don't put lids on either, because that changes how they cool. Just report the loss as a limitation of the study."),
   ("P3_DANIEL", "I'll be honest, I was worried at first that showing rounds one and two would make us look sloppy. But now I think they're actually the most interesting part. They show exactly how the definition changes the answer."),
